---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';
---

<MainLayout title="Privacy Policy | Kersivo">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 9 April 2026</p>

      <p>
        This policy describes how personal data is processed when you use websites and services operated under the
        Kersivo brand for UK barbershops, including marketing pages, demo booking and shop flows, and (where applicable)
        the barbershop admin experience. It is written in plain language and does not replace legal advice.
      </p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
      <div class="legal-placeholder">
        [TO BE COMPLETED: legal name of the data controller, registered address, country]
      </div>
      <p>
        References below to &ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo; and &ldquo;our&rdquo; mean that organisation. For data
        protection enquiries (including rights requests), contact:
      </p>
      <div class="legal-placeholder">
        [TO BE COMPLETED: contact email for privacy requests]
      </div>

      <h2>What data we process and why</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact and demo enquiries</strong> — name, email address and message content you submit through our
          contact form. <strong>Purpose:</strong> responding to your request. <strong>Typical legal basis (UK):</strong>
          steps prior to a contract and/or legitimate interests in operating our business.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Booking data</strong> — service, barber, date/time, and your contact details (name and email; phone
          if you provide it). <strong>Purpose:</strong> managing appointments, confirmations, reschedule and cancel
          links, and related emails. <strong>Typical legal basis:</strong> performance of a contract and legitimate
          interests in running the booking service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shop orders (buy-and-collect)</strong> — email address used at checkout, order contents, payment
          status as recorded after payment, and related confirmation emails. Card payments are handled by
          <strong>Stripe</strong> on the <strong>barbershop&rsquo;s own Stripe account</strong>; we do not store full
          card numbers on our servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Admin access</strong> — session cookies / tokens for authenticated access to the barbershop admin
          panel, and operational logs needed for security.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Content you upload</strong> — for example barber or product images where the product allows uploads.
          Stored so the site and shop can display them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email delivery</strong> — transactional emails (booking confirmations, order confirmations, contact
          form delivery to our inbox) are sent through an email provider (e.g. Resend) using the addresses involved in
          each message.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SMS (optional)</strong> — if you subscribe to a plan that includes SMS and we enable it for your shop,
          we may process mobile numbers and message metadata needed to send reminders or similar messages. The exact
          provider and categories will be listed here once confirmed for production.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Recipients and processors</h2>
      <p>We use service providers to host and operate the service, for example:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hosting and application runtime (e.g. Vercel or similar) in line with our deployment;</li>
        <li>Database and storage (e.g. managed PostgreSQL, object storage for images);</li>
        <li>Email delivery (e.g. Resend);</li>
        <li>Stripe, for payment processing on the barber&rsquo;s account;</li>
        <li>Future SMS provider, only where that feature is enabled.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal data. We may share data with processors strictly to provide the service, under
        appropriate agreements where required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some providers may process data outside the UK. Where that happens, we aim to rely on approved transfer tools
        (such as UK adequacy regulations or standard contractual clauses) as required by UK data protection law.
        [TO BE COMPLETED: specific sub-processors and transfers after production review]
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal data only as long as needed for the purposes above, including legal, accounting and security
        requirements. Exact retention periods depend on the type of data and your relationship with us.
        [TO BE COMPLETED: specific retention periods once internal policy is set]
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights (UK)</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to your personal data;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct inaccurate data;</li>
        <li>ask us to erase data in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to processing in certain circumstances;</li>
        <li>data portability where applicable;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To exercise these rights, contact us using the details above. You may also complain to the UK Information
        Commissioner&rsquo;s Office (ICO): <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">https://ico.org.uk/</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>
        The public marketing site does not load third-party advertising or analytics scripts by default in our
        codebase. Admin sessions use cookies (or similar) needed for login.         [TO BE COMPLETED: if you add analytics or marketing pixels, update this section and consent mechanics.]
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures appropriate to the nature of the service, including
        access controls for admin areas and encrypted connections (HTTPS) for site traffic. No online service can be
        guaranteed 100% secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date will change when we do.
        Material changes may also be communicated where appropriate (for example by email to active clients).
        [TO BE COMPLETED: preferred channel for notifying B2B clients of material changes]
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/">Back to home</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
